(Evidence Brief: Caution in Claims About the Pace and Uniformity of Warming) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Purpose) Tj
T*
(This classroom evidence brief presents methodological cautions that can support the) Tj
T*
(negative side of an overly broad proposition such as global warming is progressing) Tj
T*
(everywhere at a constant or accelerating rate. It does not claim that long-term global) Tj
T*
(warming is absent. It shows why the exact wording, time window, region, and metric) Tj
T*
(matter.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Short records and endpoint selection) Tj
T*
(Climate contains substantial year-to-year and decade-to-decade variability. Trend) Tj
T*
(estimates can change when a short record begins with an unusually warm or cool year. A) Tj
T*
(claim about acceleration requires a statistical comparison of trend rates, uncertainty) Tj
T*
(ranges, and chosen intervals. Visual inspection of a few years is not sufficient. The) Tj
T*
(negative side can challenge arguments that infer a stable rate from an arbitrary window.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Global averages and regional experience) Tj
T*
(A global mean combines areas that warm at different rates and a small number that may) Tj
T*
(cool over a chosen period. Ocean and land respond differently, and circulation can) Tj
T*
(redistribute heat. Therefore a global trend does not imply uniform local change. Claims) Tj
T*
(using words such as everywhere, every year, or uniformly are stronger than the evidence) Tj
T*
(normally supports and should be narrowed.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Measurement and reconstruction choices) Tj
T*
(Temperature products require quality control, homogenization, spatial coverage methods,) Tj
T*
(and treatment of changing instruments. Independent teams generally recover similar long-) Tj
T*
(term behavior, but individual values and short-term rankings have uncertainty. Good) Tj
T*
(debate practice is to compare datasets and uncertainty intervals, not treat one reported) Tj
T*
(decimal place as exact.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Natural variability and temporary departures) Tj
T*
(El Nino and La Nina, volcanic eruptions, solar variations, and internal ocean) Tj
T*
(circulation influence short-term surface temperature. These factors can amplify or mask) Tj
T*
(the underlying forced trend for limited periods. A temporary slowdown is not proof that) Tj
T*
(long-term warming stopped, but it can refute a simplistic claim that warming must appear) Tj
T*
(as a smooth increase in every consecutive year.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Models, scenarios, and conditional statements) Tj
T*
(Climate projections depend on future emissions, aerosol changes, land use, and model) Tj
T*
(response. Scenarios are conditional pathways rather than unconditional predictions.) Tj
T*
(Regional precipitation and extreme-event projections can have wider uncertainty than) Tj
T*
(global temperature. The negative side can legitimately challenge claims that collapse) Tj
T*
(all scenarios into one guaranteed future.) Tj
